1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:06,046
PNC's third quarter had three
headlines: an earnings beat, the
cleanest credit of six super-regional

2
00:00:06,046 --> 00:00:09,080
banks, and the thinnest capital
cushion in the group.

3
00:00:09,630 --> 00:00:15,366
Adjusted earnings per share came in
at five dollars and nine cents. That
cleared every estimate we found,

4
00:00:15,366 --> 00:00:19,904
from four ninety-one to four
ninety-eight, a beat of about two to
four percent.

5
00:00:20,454 --> 00:00:26,377
Net interest income rose fifteen
percent from a year ago, to four point
two one billion dollars, and drove

6
00:00:26,377 --> 00:00:32,358
eighty-six percent of the revenue
gain. Even so, total revenue of six
point five six billion dollars missed

7
00:00:32,358 --> 00:00:35,114
estimates by about seven tenths of a
percent.

8
00:00:35,664 --> 00:00:41,751
Credit was the bright spot. Net
charge-offs ran at just twenty-eight
basis points of loans, the lowest of

9
00:00:41,751 --> 00:00:45,310
the six banks compared. The peer
median was thirty-seven.

10
00:00:45,860 --> 00:00:51,958
Capital is the soft spot. PNC's CET1
ratio, an estimate in the release,
slipped to nine point eight percent.

11
00:00:51,958 --> 00:00:58,458
That ranks last of six, against a peer
median of ten point seven, though it
is still three point three points above

12
00:00:58,458 --> 00:01:01,642
the six and a half percent
well-capitalized minimum.

13
00:01:02,192 --> 00:01:08,333
Three things drove the quarter. The
FirstBank deal, closed in January, and
fourteen percent loan growth fed the

14
00:01:08,333 --> 00:01:14,022
margin. Fee income was soft, down
six percent from the second quarter.
And adjusted expenses rose about

15
00:01:14,022 --> 00:01:18,554
eight percent, but revenue grew
faster, so operating leverage stayed
positive.

16
00:01:19,104 --> 00:01:24,954
Looking ahead, management guided
fourth-quarter net interest income up
about four percent and adjusted

17
00:01:24,954 --> 00:01:31,271
expenses up about five percent. The
quarterly dividend rose to two dollars
from one seventy, and consensus for

18
00:01:31,271 --> 00:01:34,446
next quarter is five dollars and ten
cents a share.

19
00:01:34,996 --> 00:01:41,412
The open question is whether PNC
can keep growing while it rebuilds
capital toward its ten percent target.

20
00:01:41,412 --> 00:01:47,090
As CFO Rob Reilly put it, we continue
to demonstrate strong momentum
across the franchise.

